  "notes": [
    "Eight independently drawn views mechanically packed without horizontal reflection. Generated source and layout provenance are saved in art/sister-source-layout.json.",
    "Anatomical right hand holds the staff, and the staff remains part of the fixed torso image.",
    "Opaque white leggings are extracted as distinct legs. Occluded profile and rear-diagonal far legs reuse one complete unreflected symmetric leg texture, rather than stretching the visible heel-only fragment; no second shoe is included in the source mask.",
    "Long hair, tunic hem and blue-green side panels are fixed occlusion layers over the moving legs.",
    "The submitted reference costume could not be edited through image generation due to an output safety rejection. This asset uses a covered white-and-gold tunic, opaque leggings and sleeves; it is an alternate costume, not an exact reproduction.",
    "The front gold side hairpin appears on anatomical left in this generated alternate design, unlike the original reference annotation.",
    "Leg texturePolygon boundaries follow the actual tunic hem and exclude fixed gold hems, teal panels and far-leg slivers. hipRimBleed is zero. Explicit pinSpan binds the upper leg smoothly without retaining a fixed strip of the old standing leg; top occlusion polygons follow the garment outline rather than a rectangular band."
